          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Cnidium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Apiaceae, native to Eurasia and North America."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Species\n{{As of|2022|December}}, Plants of the World Online accepted the following species:\nCnidium bhutanicum M.F.Watson\nCnidium cnidiifolium (Turcz.) Schischk.\nCnidium dauricum (Jacq.) Fisch. & C.A.Mey.\nCnidium divaricatum (Jacq.) Ledeb.\nCnidium japonicum Miq.\nCnidium monnieri (L.) Cusson\nCnidium silaifolium (Jacq.) Simonk.\nCnidium warburgii H.Wolff"
          }
        ]
      },
